<title>FRANCE: US buy to boost St Gobain result from 97.</title>
<headline>US buy to boost St Gobain result from 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French glassmaker Saint-Gobain said on Monday the acquisition of a 42 percent stake in Ball Foster from Ball Corporation for $190 million would have a positive impact on Saint-Gobain's net result from 1997.  </p>
<p>&quot;It is forecast the operation will have a positive impact on the group's net result from 1997,&quot; Saint-Gobain said in a statement.</p>
<p>U.S. glass maker Ball Foster was founded in 1995 by Saint-Gobain and Ball Corporation, each holding 58 percent and 42 percent respectively,</p>
<p>Saint-Gobain shares were steady at 660 francs at 1300 GMT, up two on the day.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
